meta {
  name: Get Donation Records
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/donate/records?page=&limit=&orderBy=&search=&sortBy=
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  page: 
  limit: 
  orderBy: 
  search: 
  sortBy: 
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Get Donation Records
  
  Returns a paginated list of donation records from the `donors` table. Results can be sorted by multiple fields and filtered by a full-text search query.
  
  ## Endpoint
  `GET /api/v1/donate`
  
  ## Authorization
  
  - **Authentication:** Required — Bearer token via `authenticate()`.
  - **Permission:** `update` — enforced by `authorize("update")`.
  
  ## Request
  
  ### Query Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type   | Required | Default     | Description / Allowed Values                                                                                     |
  |-----------|--------|----------|-------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `page`    | number | No       | `1`         | Page number (integer ≥ 1)                                                                                        |
  | `limit`   | number | No       | `25`        | Items per page (integer, 1–100)                                                                                  |
  | `orderBy` | string | No       | `desc`      | Sort direction. One of: `asc`, `desc`                                                                            |
  | `sortBy`  | string | No       | `createdAt` | Field to sort by. One of: `name`, `amount`, `email`, `createdAt`                                                 |
  | `search`  | string | No       | —           | Full-text search query. When provided, cache is bypassed and results are matched against the text search vector. |
  
  ### Searchable Fields
  
  Full-text search queries match against the following columns using PostgreSQL text search:
  
  | Field     | Weight |
  |-----------|--------|
  | `name`    | A      |
  | `email`   | A      |
  | `comment` | C      |
  
  Plain text amount search is also performed using a fallback ILIKE comparison.
  
  ## Response
  
  **`200 OK`** — Returns a paginated list of donation records.
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Found all donation records successfully",
    "data": [
      {
        "id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
        "amount": 900,
        "name": "John Doe",
        "email": "donor@example.com",
        "supportAreas": ["FUND_BOOTCAMP", "SPONSOR_ASH_BENEFICIARY"],
        "comment": "Love your work",
        "metaData": "{...}",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-10T12:00:00.000Z"
      }
    ],
    "meta": {
      "pagination": {
        "page": 1,
        "limit": 25,
        "totalPages": 1
      },
      "correlationId": "uuid-v4-string"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Caching
  
  - **Cache Key:** `cedarrise:clientside:donations:{page}:{limit}:{orderBy}:{sortBy}`
  - **TTL:** 10 minutes (600 seconds — `LISTS`)
  - **Bypass:** Caching is bypassed entirely when a `search` query parameter is provided.
  
  ## Errors
  
  | Status                      | Description                                                  |
  |-----------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `400 Bad Request`           | Invalid query parameters (e.g. invalid `sortBy` or `limit`). |
  | `401 Unauthorized`          | Missing or invalid Bearer token.                             |
  | `403 Forbidden`             | Insufficient permissions.                                    |
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected server error.                                     |
}
